# Testing

| What is tested                                  | Project                     | File                         |
| ----------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Entities, value objects, use cases              | `backend/tests/unit`        | `<layer>/<feature>/*.spec.ts` |
| HTTP endpoints end to end                       | `backend/tests/integration` | `<feature>/*.int-spec.ts`    |
| Isolated components and utilities               | `frontend/tests/unit`       | `*.test.tsx`                 |
| Full features (form + hook + mocked API)        | `frontend/tests/integration`| `*.test.tsx`                 |
| Critical user flows, real frontend + backend    | `frontend/tests/e2e`        | `<flow>/*.spec.ts`           |

Test folder structure mirrors the source structure.

## Backend

- Unit: no Nest, no IO. Use the fakes in `backend/tests/unit/fakes` (add new ones there), not Jest mocks for repositories.
- Integration: boot the app with `createTestApp()` (uses `AppModule` + `setupApp`) and test with Supertest. Cover the happy path, 400 validation, 404 and 409.

## Frontend

- Render with `renderWithProviders` (QueryClient + Router).
- Query by role or label (`getByRole`, `getByLabelText`), never by CSS class or test id when an accessible alternative exists.
- Mock the network with `vi.spyOn(globalThis, 'fetch')`.

## E2E (Playwright)

- Critical flows only (few and valuable); edge cases belong in unit/integration.
- No mocks: tests hit the real backend started by `playwright.config.ts`.
- Accessible locators (`getByRole`, `getByLabel`) and web-first assertions (`await expect(locator).toBeVisible()`); never `waitForTimeout`.
- Tests are independent: unique data via `uniqueEmail()` from `tests/e2e/support`; seed state through the API (`request.post`) instead of the UI.

## Style

- One behavior per `it`, named in present tense describing the outcome: `it('throws NotFoundError when the user does not exist')`.
- Arrange / Act / Assert separated by a blank line.
